{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the first came out ruddy.</b> They said in the Midrash: in the merit of ״ולקחתם לכם ביום הראשון״ — 'and you shall take for yourselves on the first day' — I reveal Myself to you first, and I exact retribution from the first, and I build for you the first, and I bring to you the first. I reveal Myself to you first, as it is said (Isaiah 44:6): ״אני ראשון ואני אחרון״; and I exact retribution from the first — this is Esau the wicked, as it is said: ״ויצא הראשון אדמוני״; and I build for you the first — this is the Temple, as it is said (Jeremiah 17:12): ״כסא כבוד מרום מראשון״; and I bring to you the first — this is King Messiah, as it is said (Isaiah 41:27): ״ראשון לציון הנה הנם ולירושלים מבשר אתן״." "<b>All of him like a hairy mantle.</b> The meaning is: all of him was hair, like a mantle, for so he was born. And therefore he was called איש שעיר (a hairy man), which includes both the hair (שער) and the goats (שעירים), which belong to the aspect of strength (כח) that is his. And so they said in the Midrash: his strength — he has hair corresponding to his heart, and in the time of the redemption that hair will fall at the sounding of the shofar, as it is said (Zechariah 9:14): ״וה׳ אלהים בשופר יתקע והלך בסערות תימן״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:04.947378023Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}